'' vendor/mariadb -- MariaDB Connector/C 3.4.11, the C client library for MySQL and MariaDB
'' servers (the mysql.h API), as one import:
''
''     #import "vendor/mariadb" link dynamic        (or no 'link': there is only a shared library)
''
'' Every routine, type and constant of mysql.h is then callable as MariaDB and MySQL document
'' it, unqualified -- mysql_init, mysql_real_connect, mysql_stmt_prepare, MYSQL_BIND,
'' MYSQL_OPT_SSL_CA. It connects to MariaDB and to MySQL 5.7, 8 and later: every login plugin
'' is built in -- mysql_native_password, caching_sha2_password (MySQL 8's default) and
'' sha256_password, client_ed25519 and parsec (MariaDB's).
''
'' THE HEADER is mariadb.ti, translated by 'tiko c2t' and committed. mysql.h is six headers
'' that only work together, so flatten.py first writes them as one -- mariadb.h, the file the
'' banner names by SHA-256 -- and c2t translates that. mariadb-residue.ti holds by hand what the
'' translation could not carry; above all MYSQL, which is OPAQUE here: hold the MYSQL ptr that
'' mysql_init returns and ask the API for what is in it.
''
'' A query with a parameter, through a prepared statement -- never splice values into SQL text:
''
''     dim as MYSQL ptr m = mysql_init( nullptr )
''     if mysql_real_connect( m, "db.example.com", "app", pw, "app", 3306, nullptr, 0 ) = nullptr then
''         print *mysql_error( m ) : end 1
''     end if
''     mysql_set_character_set( m, "utf8mb4" )
''     dim as MYSQL_STMT ptr st = mysql_stmt_init( m )
''     dim as string sql = "update item set price = ? where id = ?"
''     mysql_stmt_prepare( st, strptr( sql ), len( sql ) )
''     ... a MYSQL_BIND per '?', mysql_stmt_bind_param, mysql_stmt_execute ...
''     mysql_stmt_close( st ) : mysql_close( m )
''
'' What the library allocates, the library frees: mysql_close (also after a failed connect),
'' mysql_free_result, mysql_stmt_close. A MYSQL_ROW lives as long as its MYSQL_RES.
''
'' TLS: Connector/C 3.4 uses TLS whenever the server offers it, and checks the server's
'' certificate against MYSQL_OPT_SSL_CA when that is set (with MYSQL_OPT_SSL_VERIFY_SERVER_CERT).
'' On Windows it is Schannel's; on Linux and macOS, OpenSSL's, inside the library -- nothing else to ship.
''
'' THE LIBRARY is shared only -- Connector/C is LGPL-2.1, so a program's user must be able to
'' replace it -- and tiko copies it beside the program: libmariadb.dll on Windows,
'' libmariadb_linux_x86_64.so or libmariadb_linux_arm64.so on Linux, libmariadb_macos_arm64.dylib
'' on macOS. 'link static' is refused (pkg/vendor/tiko.toml).
#module "mariadb"

public #include once "mariadb-residue.ti"
public #include once "mariadb.ti"

#foreignlib MARIADB dynamic "lib/libmariadb"
